course: dictionary
lesson: 2582
title: Which meaning fits?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer wants. «Foxes raise their cubs in a den under the roots of a tree.» Here den is a home for a wild animal, because the foxes raise their cubs in it. The word den on its own could mean many things, so the words around it are the clue.
explain: «The children built a den in the garden from sticks and an old blanket.» Now den means a secret hideout that children make, because they built it from sticks and a blanket. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some dens are not places you can visit at all. «The gang was a den of thieves» means a place where bad things happen in secret. Stories also use «into the lion's den» to mean a scary place. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A den can be a home for a wild animal, often hidden away.
fact: A den can also be a secret hideout that children build from sticks, blankets or boxes.
fact: A den can mean a small, cosy room in a house, mainly used in America.
fact: A den can mean a place where bad things happen in secret, as in «a den of thieves».
fact: A badger's home is called a sett, and bears sleep through winter in dens.
exercise: «Foxes raise their cubs in a den under the roots of a tree.» What does den mean here? | *A wild animal's hidden home | A place where thieves plan crimes | A small cosy room in a house | A secret hideout built from sticks
exercise: «The children built a den in the garden from sticks and an old blanket.» What does den mean here? | A shop that sells blankets | A wild animal's home | *A secret hideout that children make | A room for watching television
exercise: «The gang was a den of thieves, meeting in secret.» What does den mean in this sentence? | A wild animal's home | A cosy room for reading | A school for young children | *A place where bad things happen in secret
test: «Bears sleep through winter in dens, living on their fat.» Which best describes a den here? | A busy kitchen | *A hidden home where a bear rests through winter | A party game for children | A shop for fur coats
test: «Dad's den is a small cosy room where he reads in the evening.» What does den mean? | A secret hideout made of sticks | A busy kitchen where dinner is cooked | *A small cosy room in a house | A hidden cave for wolves
exam: «Going to the dentist felt like walking into the lion's den.» What does den mean here? | *A scary place | A secret hideout made of sticks | A small cosy room in a house | A fox's home under a tree
